    <!-- Detailed Guide -->
    <string name="guide_welcome">Protecting your privacy is our mission. Follow this guide to master Glasses Scanner.</string>
    <string name="guide_1_title">1. Real-time Scanner</string>
    <string name="guide_1_desc">The scanner uses Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) to detect smart glasses. The central Radar visualizes the signal search. Tap any device to see advanced signal trends.</string>
    <string name="guide_2_title">2. Proximity Levels</string>
    <string name="guide_2_desc">IMMEDIATE (&lt; 1m): The device is on a person right next to you. \nNEAR (&lt; 3m): The device is within the same room. \nFAR (&gt; 5m): Signal is weak, possibly in an adjacent room.</string>
    <string name="guide_3_title">3. AI Visual Scan</string>
    <string name="guide_3_desc">Use the AI Scan tab to find hidden cameras. Point your camera at someone\\\'s glasses; it helps you spot the tiny LED flicker that indicates a recording is in progress.</string>
    <string name="guide_4_title">4. Zone Security</string>
    <string name="guide_4_desc">Activate Zone Mode in sensitive areas (meeting rooms, changing rooms). It increases scan frequency and automatically tags every detection as a priority audit.</string>
    <string name="guide_5_title">5. Device Tagging</string>
    <string name="guide_5_desc">Identified a friend\\\'s glasses? Use the Edit icon to tag them (e.g., \"Andi\\\'s Ray-Bans\"). This helps you ignore known devices and focus on unknown threats.</string>

